  "verdict": {
    "outcome": "O14",
    "direction": "worsens",
    "magnitude": "moderate",
    "time_horizon": "this-parliament",
    "confidence": "moderate",
    "plain": "This stamp duty cut delivers the largest cash savings to buyers of more expensive homes, so it disproportionately benefits wealthier households. Evidence also suggests a significant share of any saving gets absorbed into higher house prices, which can hurt less wealthy buyers most.",
    "biggest_unknown": "How much of the tax saving is captured by sellers as higher prices rather than retained by buyers \u2014 if the price-inflation effect is large, the regressive distributional harm is compounded; if supply responds strongly, it is partly offset.",
